> consecutive clicks to be interpreted as a double click.

You may also click on the space you're on, if there's a dungeon feature 
there. For example, if you're standing on a chest, you'll try to open 
it, and when you're on stairs, you'll take them.

>      Travel mode via mouse click can be turned off via the 'O'
> command or OPTIONS=noTravel

That will not only turn off mouse travel, but travel mode completely (ie 
the _-command won't work any longer, either).

Also, the mouse can still operate as described above (clicking on a 
chest while standing there still works.

A better way to turn off mouse travel is to leave travel alone, but set 
OPTIONS=NoMouse_Support

